                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I really tried to like this game, because I'm also a developer, and I love tycoons. It's just.. I won't judge it for bugs, because it's of course an alpha, but I will judge it's gameplay.\n\nFirst of all, I don't like playing scenarios in this kind of games, so I went straight for sandbox. I've chosen 40.000$ for start, rented the moderate place, hired moderate worker, bought moderate coffe machine, bought ingredients.. And if it's all moderate, (not cheap at all) then it should be quite alright, shouldn't be?\n\nBut then suddenly my worker at his first day of work got ill, his performance dropped to 5%, energy to 0. The next day he was okey, but as the night came my kiosk got vandalized, and after that night my worker got ill again. 2 days after - kiosk got vandalized again. It's just.. If it's a tycoon, give a little room to breathe, I would like to see my first income. (Opinions were B  so it wasn't bad but sales were horrible). And I tried couple of times.. It's always the same, workers are ill 2-3 times a week and kiosk is being vandalized in same frequency.\n\nAnd about leveling up workers, experience grows way to slow..",
                        "timestamp_created": 1541333968,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1541333968,
                        "voted_up": false,
                        "votes_up": 35,
                        "votes_funny": 6,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.7130658030509949,
                        "comment_count": 9,
                        "steam_purchase": true,
                        "received_for_free": false,
                        "written_during_early_access": true,
                        "developer_response": "Thanks for your review. It seems for me like a bug. There should not be so many bad events like you described. I’ll check it out. Also, I am planning to add configurable events chances in the sandbox and add “cooldown” time for events. I hope you will give CoffeeBiz one more chance after some updates.",
